      "foundry": "Martin Majoor",
      "designer": "Martin Majoor",
      "description": "Scala: a typefaces that changed the world.\n\nScala® was launched in November 1989, designed exclusively for Music Centre Vredenburg in Utrecht. A year later, it was released by FontShop International in Berlin, becoming the first serious text typeface on the FontFont label. The award-winning Scala has since become a worldwide bestseller and is regarded as a 'digital classic'. In 2013, London's Design Museum selected Scala as one of the 'Fifty Typefaces that Changed the World'.\n\nScala’s already huge success was bolstered by the arrival of Scala Sans in 1993. The sans was based primarily on Scala, making it a humanist sans, complete with a real italic, rather than a merely slanted roman.",
